{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "azerty-fr",
  "name": "AZERTY (French)",
  "isDefault": false,
  "language": "fr",
  "order": 0,
  "about": "The French layout's key inventory for Hexboard, transcribed from FlorisBoard (Apache 2.0): the letter rows from app/src/main/assets/ime/keyboard/org.florisboard.layouts/layouts/characters/azerty.json and the long-press accents from app/src/main/assets/ime/keyboard/org.florisboard.localization/popupMappings/fr.json, both read on 2026-09-05. FlorisBoard's third row ends in an apostrophe; Hexboard's row 3 already carries one, so only the letters are taken from that row and the freed slots hold the structural keys. The RARE and SYMBOLS panels and row 3 of the home panel are copied unchanged from resources/key-layout.json: none of them is language-specific, and the two space bars, the shift key and the common punctuation are Hexboard's own rather than any keyboard's. Geometry is deliberately absent — the zag rule, the circle sizing and the nearest-centre hit-testing live in Kotlin, because they are the perceptual wedge SPEC calls inviolable. resources/key-manifest-fr.md is generated from this file by scripts/generate-key-manifest.py and must not be hand-edited.",
  "generates": "resources/key-manifest-fr.md",
  "manifestRules": [
    "NO KEY MAY BE LOST. Every output character must appear in this manifest. Before shipping any build, run audit_keys.js and confirm the output set matches exactly.",
    "NO UNRESOLVED DUPLICATES. Each output character should appear on exactly one panel. Cross-panel duplicates must be resolved before shipping — either remove one instance and fill the vacated slot with something new, or explicitly justify why both are needed (e.g. a convenience copy that is clearly labelled).",
    "NO SILENT CHANGES. Any key move, addition, or removal must be reflected in this manifest and noted in the commit comment.",
    "EMPTY SLOTS ARE OPPORTUNITIES, NOT ACCEPTABLE GAPS. If a duplicate is removed, the freed slot must be filled with a character that has no other home, agreed with the user first."
  ],
  "rule1Note": "Rule 1 names `audit_keys.js`, which is a browser-prototype script. The wording is kept as written because it describes the prototype. The underlying principle — verify the shipped key set against this manifest before shipping — is what carries over to Android, where the mechanism will be different.",
  "nonConsumers": [
    "hexboard17.html — the browser prototype. Frozen: reference only, does not read this config.",
    "planning/layout-preview.html — the standing layout preview fixture. Does not read this config either; it stays hand-edited per CLAUDE.md."
  ],
